# Build output. Everything under build/ is generated by the Makefile — the
# allocator's emitted .inc files, the assembled .o/.sfc ROMs, and the generated
# assets. Nothing here is tracked.
#
# (No force-tracked exceptions: every file under build/ has a recipe that
# makes it. The one artifact that had none — a pre-built sky gradient — lives
# under vendor/probe_ref/ instead, so build/ here is genuinely disposable.)
build/

# Repo-local MesenCore cache, written by tools/setup.sh. Multi-MB binary.
tools/Mesen/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Measurement + screenshot scratch
*.png
!docs/**/*.png
# Vendored font bitmaps are source assets, not build output. Without this the
# blanket *.png above makes `git add -A` a SILENT partial success — it swallowed
# a font vendoring attempt on 2026-07-28 (docs/11_font_assets.md §4).
!vendor/fonts/*.png
# ...and vendored SOURCE ART, for exactly the same reason and after exactly the
# same failure. On 2026-08-02 the blanket rule above swallowed
# vendor/art/spaceship_pack/*.png (the shmup rail's source PNGs): `git add -A`
# reported nothing, `git status` was clean, the local build was green, and CI
# failed on a bare runner with `FileNotFoundError: .../planet_1.png`. That is
# the SECOND occurrence of the class this block already documents. The lesson
# recorded in docs/11 §4 was "add a negation" — the lesson now is that a
# blanket ignore for a file type the repo legitimately vendors keeps costing a
# CI round trip, and every new vendored-asset directory needs its negation
# added in the same commit that creates it.
!vendor/art/**/*.png

# Agent worktrees, created by the Claude Code harness when an agent is
# dispatched with worktree isolation. Each is a full checkout of this repo
# inside this repo (~5 MB), ephemeral, and removed when the agent finishes —
# committing one would nest the tree inside itself.
#
# Narrow on purpose: .claude/ itself holds TRACKED project config here
# (.claude/hooks/, .claude/settings.json), so only the worktrees path is
# ignored. Missing this line once was enough to have a worktree trip the stop
# hook, which is why it is spelled out rather than assumed.
.claude/worktrees/

# make determinism FALSIFY=1 plants a throwaway module copy here;
# a crashed run must not dirty the tree.
tests/planted_determinism_*.py
